plugin-qualify (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * npm publish: run by hand until the name exists on npm
  * README: install from the FreeMixer channel
  * Comments no longer cite the private tree
  * README: install states only what exists
  * ci: no changelog job; git history is the changelog
  * Remove CHANGELOG.md and the checks that read it
  * BUILDING.md: the test suite needs Node.js 20
  * Run on the Node.js that Debian ships: require Node.js 18, not 22
  * CI: the pack check can no longer SIGPIPE tar
  * npm trusted publishing on a tag, RPM and DEB release workflow, package
    dry run in CI
  * RPM spec and debian/ packaging, generated changelogs
  * Changelog entry for 0.1.1
  * README installs from the FreeMixer channel, docs cite no private specs
  * Rename the package to @openmixer/plugin-qualify, keep bytecode out of the
    tarball
  * ci: the pack check lists the tarball into a file, so a grep that stops
    early cannot SIGPIPE tar under pipefail

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:16:57 +0000
